  "rating": {
    "inherent": "high",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "high",
    "rationale": "Present risk is a property finding, not an untrusted-input attack path: only trusted on-call engineers can invoke the assistant, but the design lacks attributable provenance because the agent acts with the engineer's personal token and writes production actions to the cloud audit log under the engineer's identity alone. Under rubric section 5a, the affected capabilities include an irreversible production database migration, so the highest sink class is S3 and the inherent tier is high using the I-row base for missing properties. Declared controls limit access and record actions, but they do not restore attribution or create an immutable linkage from request to action, so residual remains high. Forecast also remains high because no present control is the one that would lower this finding; the missing structural provenance controls are recommended but not yet implemented. Manual validation applied against the checklist because scripts could not be run."
  },
